      <h2>One Trusted Team. Every Type of L31 Home.</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">Maghull is almost entirely a 20th-century town. Semi-detached and detached on planned estates. Here's what we usually find.</p>
      <div class="pf-why-grid" style="margin-top:2rem;">

        <details class="pf-why-item m-acc"><summary><h3>1930s and 1940s Pre-War Semis</h3></summary><p>The earliest stock of modern Maghull, built when the Northway opened in 1933 and the town started growing. Bay windows, three-bed family layouts. Copper pipework and heating systems all replaced two or three times since.</p></details>

        <details class="pf-why-item m-acc"><summary><h3>1950s and 1960s Post-War Estates</h3></summary><p>Maghull's population went from 10,000 in 1951 to 22,000 by 1971. Most of the housing dates from that boom. Original pipework now 60 to 70 years old. Pinhole leaks and corroded cylinder connections are common.</p></details>

        <details class="pf-why-item m-acc"><summary><h3>1970s and 1980s Private Estates</h3></summary><p>The dormitory boom era. Detached and semi-detached on quiet streets off Deyes Lane, School Lane and Park Lane. System boilers, hot water cylinders, three-port valves. We carry common parts.</p></details>

        <details class="pf-why-item m-acc"><summary><h3>Modern Sefton East New Builds</h3></summary><p>The 2010s Sefton East housing zone added new estates around Maghull. Modern combi boilers, push-fit plumbing, often still under maker warranty. We honour warranty terms when we work.</p></details>

        <details class="pf-why-item m-acc"><summary><h3>McCarthy & Stone Retirement Living</h3></summary><p>The Royal British Legion site on Liverpool Road South is now 44 retirement flats. More retirement schemes across town. Shared boiler systems, communal hot water. We work with managing agents.</p></details>

        <details class="pf-why-item m-acc"><summary><h3>Canalside and Old Village Period Properties</h3></summary><p>The old village core near Red Lion Bridge and the Leeds and Liverpool Canal has older Victorian and Edwardian stock. Lead supply pipes, cast iron waste, mixed-era upgrades. We know the patchwork.</p></details>

      </div>
    </div>
